---
source: crates/ledger-mcp/src/tools.rs
expression: "all.join(\"\\n\")"
---
claim_inadmissible [claim]: memory layout needs a type name and non-zero size. Next: Fix the claim and propose it again.
premise_unknown [0123abcd]: No claim has this id. Next: Propose the premise first, or drop it from this claim.
evidence_unknown [0123abcd]: No evidence has this id. Next: Call add_evidence with the capture file first.
evidence_wrong_kind [HttpExchange]: This kind of evidence cannot check this kind of claim. Next: The claim is filed but unchecked. Propose it again with evidence of the right kind and format.
evidence_malformed [f9060556d6f5]: The file is not in the format its kind requires. Next: The claim is filed but unchecked. Propose it again with evidence of the right kind and format.
evidence_not_applicable [6cfbecad6ee9]: It is `POST https://game.example/score`, which the claim says nothing about. Next: The claim is filed but unchecked. Replay only evidence the claim is about: captures of its endpoint and status, or an analysis that recovered its caller.
key_unknown [0123abcd]: No evidence has this id. Next: Add the key file with add_evidence kind=secret and cite its id as `key`.
key_not_secret [6cfbecad6ee9]: This evidence is not of kind secret. Next: Add the key file with add_evidence kind=secret and cite its id as `key`.
claim_inadmissible [claim]: an endpoint is written `METHOD [host]/path`, like `GET api.example.com/users/{id}`. Next: Fix the claim and propose it again.
argument_missing [claim]: about=claim needs `claim`. Next: Call ask again with that argument.
argument_missing [subject]: about=subject needs `subject`. Next: Call ask again with that argument.
claim_unknown [0123abcd]: No claim has this id. Next: Use ask with about=all to list claims, or propose the claim first.
claim_unknown [0123abcd]: No claim has this id. Next: Use ask with about=all to list claims, or propose the claim first.
claim_unknown []: No claim has this id. Next: Use ask with about=all to list claims, or propose the claim first.
claim_unknown [0123abcd]: No claim has this id. Next: Use ask with about=all to list claims, or propose the claim first.
evidence_unreadable [path]: No such file or directory (os error 2). Next: Check that the path is a local file this server can read.
evidence_other_kind [3806d4b7938d]: These bytes are already stored as secret, and stored evidence keeps its kind. Next: Nothing was recorded. Cite the evidence under the kind it has, or tell the human if that kind is wrong.
claim_unknown []: No claim has this id. Next: Use ask with about=all to list claims, or propose the claim first.
claim_unknown []: No claim has this id. Next: Use ask with about=all to list claims, or propose the claim first.
evidence_unknown []: No evidence has this id. Next: Call add_evidence with the capture file first.
evidence_unreadable [path]: It is not a regular file. Next: Check that the path is a local file this server can read.
evidence_too_large [path]: 268435457 bytes, limit 268435456. Next: Nothing was recorded. Give a smaller file, such as a HAR file of fewer requests, or tell the human.
evidence_too_large [path]: 16777217 bytes, limit 16777216. Next: Nothing was recorded. Give a smaller file, such as a HAR file of fewer requests, or tell the human.
